--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- cross-flow VIV lock-in of a taut line in a uniform cross current, 90 s
-- A 100 m line (D 0.1 m, 10 kg/m, EA 5e7 N, about 50 kN) held at both ends 50 m below the
-- surface in a 0.15 m/s current along +Y, across the line. The LINE TYPES columns Cl dF cF give
-- the lift coefficient 0.8 and MoorDyn's synchronisation band (dF 0.08 around cF 0.18): the
-- shedding frequency cF U/D = 0.27 Hz sits on the first vertical mode (0.27 Hz with the added
-- mass), so the line locks in and vibrates in Z, across the flow: over 60-90 s the mid-span
-- amplitude A/D is 0.66, MoorDyn-F's on this line (tests/test_viv_lockin.py). L1N26pz is the
-- mid-span node, L1N13pz the quarter span; the Outputs flag V writes the lift at every node to
-- <root>.Line1.V.out.
-- VIVphaseSeed spread starts node i at the phase 2 pi i/N (MoorDyn-C); VIVrmsWindow sets the
-- averaging time of the running RMS motion of the synchronisation model. The static start
-- carries the current drag but no lift; the lift builds up from the seeded phases.
